#### builds counter ui and applies deterministic transitions

- Verify: builds counter ui and applies deterministic transitions
   - Expected: ui.root_id equals `root`
   - Expected: inc.value equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: inc.status equals `incremented`
   - Expected: app.value equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 10 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: builds counter ui and applies deterministic transitions")
var app = CounterApp.new()
val ui = app.build_ui()
expect(ui.root_id).to_equal("root")
val inc = counter_apply_action(app.value, "counter_increment")
expect(inc.value).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(inc.status).to_equal("incremented")
app.handle_event(UIEvent.Action(name: "counter_increment"))
expect(app.value).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement
```

</details>

### Office Hardening

#### adds slides image element without fake asset path

- Verify: adds slides image element without fake asset path
   - Expected: slide.elements.len() equals `2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: image_src equals ``
   - Expected: image_alt equals `Image Frame`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 17 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: adds slides image element without fake asset path")
var app = SlidesApp.new()
app.handle_event(UIEvent.Action(name: "add_image"))
val slide = current_slide(app.presentation)
expect(slide.elements.len()).to_equal(2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement
var image_src = "<not-image>"
var image_alt = "<not-image>"
match slide.elements[slide.elements.len() - 1].kind:
    SlideElementKind.ImageEl(src: src, alt: alt):
        image_src = src
        image_alt = alt
    _:
        image_src = "<not-image>"
        image_alt = "<not-image>"
expect(image_src).to_equal("")
expect(image_alt).to_equal("Image Frame")
```

</details>

